  "title": "A finite-width enumeration of ascent sequences avoiding 0120 and 0121",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For the exact class A_n frozen in source.md and defined in problem.md (all nonnegative ascent sequences with x_1=0, x_i<=1+asc(x_1...x_(i-1)), simultaneously avoiding classical equality-preserving subsequences 0120 and 0121, with A_0={empty}), the following gives its all-length uniform structural enumeration. For K>=2 set D_K={(k,H):2<=k<=K, empty!=H subset {0,...,k-2}}. For s=(k,H), m=min(H), and 0<=t<k, set f(s,t)=(k,H union {t}) if t<=m; otherwise set r=|{h in H:h<t}| and f(s,t)=(k+1-r,{h-r:h in H,h>=t} union {t-r}). Define T_K(s,u)=|{t:f(s,t)=u}|, the row b_K to have value 1 on (K,{h}) for 0<=h<=K-2 and 0 elsewhere, and the column 1 to be all ones. Then, as an identity in Z[[z]], F(z)=sum_(n>=0)|A_n|z^n=(1-z)/(1-2z)+sum_(K>=2)(z/(1-z))^(2K-1) b_K(I-zT_K)^(-1)1. Equivalently, for n>=1, |A_n|=2^(n-1)+sum_(K=2)^floor((n+1)/2) sum_(d=0)^(n-2K+1) binom(n-d-1,2K-2)b_K T_K^d 1, and |A_0|=1. The eligible-rank quotient and binary initialization underlying these formulas hold for every prefix, width never increases after the first letter >=2, |D_K|=2^K-K-1, and only K<=floor((N+1)/2) is needed through degree N. The claimed resolution uses the original uniform-structural-enumeration alternative; no simpler scalar closed form, rationality or algebraicity of F, or nonzero analytic convergence radius is asserted.",
